import Mathlib

-- Declarations for this item will be appended below by the statement pipeline.

universe u v

section

variable {G : Type u} [Group G] {ι : Type v}

/-
Layer triage:
- `source-facing`: two indexed families `g g' : ι → G` and the existence of one overgroup element
  simultaneously conjugating every `g i` to `g' i` after embedding `G`.
- `core/canonical`: `Subgroup.closure (Set.range g)`, `Subgroup.closure (Set.range g')`, and
  mathlib's HNN owner `HNNExtension G A B φ` with `HNNExtension.of`, `HNNExtension.t`,
  `HNNExtension.equiv_eq_conj`, and `HNNExtension.of_injective`.
- `bridge/view`: an isomorphism between the two generated subgroups carrying the canonical members
  `g i` to `g' i`; the reverse implication realizes the desired overgroup by the HNN extension.

Domain sampling:
1. `HNNExtension G A B φ` is mathlib's owner abstraction for adjoining one stable letter that
   conjugates the subgroup `A` onto `B` through the isomorphism `φ`.
2. `HNNExtension.of` and `HNNExtension.of_injective` provide the canonical embedding of the base
   group into that owner.
3. `HNNExtension.t` and `HNNExtension.equiv_eq_conj` encode the defining conjugation relation for
   the stable letter.
4. `Subgroup.closure (Set.range g)` is the canonical owner for the subgroup `Gp{g_i}` generated by
   the family `g`.

Primitive vs. derived:
the primitive source data are only the two families `g` and `g'`. The generated subgroups are
derived canonically as closures of their ranges, and the ambient overgroup in the reverse
direction is derived from the HNN owner construction, so no extra wrapper structure belongs in the
public API.
-/
/-- Proposition 1-6-2: a group can be embedded in an overgroup containing one element that
simultaneously conjugates every `g i` to `g' i` if and only if the generated subgroups
`Gp{g_i}` and `Gp{g_i'}` are isomorphic by a map carrying each `g i` to `g' i`. -/
-- Proof sketch: if `f : G →* H` is injective and `x⁻¹ * f (g i) * x = f (g' i)` for every `i`,
-- then conjugation by `x` restricts to an isomorphism between the images of the two generated
-- subgroups, and injectivity of `f` transports that isomorphism back to
-- `Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) ≃* Subgroup.closure (Set.range g')`. Conversely, given such an
-- isomorphism `φ`, take the owner HNN extension
-- `HNNExtension G (Subgroup.closure (Set.range g)) (Subgroup.closure (Set.range g')) φ`; the
-- canonical embedding `HNNExtension.of` is injective, and the stable letter `HNNExtension.t⁻¹`
-- satisfies `x⁻¹ * of (g i) * x = of (g' i)` by `HNNExtension.equiv_eq_conj`. That owner lives in
-- the same universe as `G`, so no extra ambient-universe parameter is needed in the public
-- statement.
theorem exists_embedding_with_common_conjugator_iff
    (g g' : ι → G) :
    (∃ (H : Type u) (_ : Group H) (f : G →* H) (x : H),
      Function.Injective f ∧ ∀ i, x⁻¹ * f (g i) * x = f (g' i)) ↔
      ∃ φ : Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) ≃* Subgroup.closure (Set.range g'),
        ∀ i, (φ ⟨g i, Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_range_self i)⟩ : G) = g' i := sorry

end
